  "product_title": "Multi-list task manager for Google Tasks refugees",
  "architecture_overview": {
    "diagram_description": "iOS client (SwiftUI) talks to a thin FastAPI backend for auth, sync, and Google import jobs. PostgreSQL stores users/lists/tasks; Redis queues import workers; optional local-only mode keeps tasks on-device until Pro sync is enabled. Waitlist is a static Next.js page posting to the same API.",
    "key_components": [
      {
        "name": "iOS SwiftUI client",
        "responsibility": "Multi-list sidebar, archive/search UI, StoreKit paywall, offline-first task editing"
      },
      {
        "name": "FastAPI sync & import API",
        "responsibility": "Auth, CRUD sync, Google OAuth import jobs, calendar sync webhooks"
      },
      {
        "name": "PostgreSQL + Redis",
        "responsibility": "Durable task data and async import/worker queue with retries"
      },
      {
        "name": "Waitlist web (Next.js)",
        "responsibility": "Capture switch-intent emails and list-count for interviews before App Store launch"
      }
    ],
    "data_flow": "User edits tasks on device \u2192 local SQLite mirror \u2192 sync API upserts to Postgres when online. Import flow: OAuth \u2192 enqueue Redis job \u2192 worker pulls Google Tasks pages \u2192 writes lists/tasks \u2192 client polls job status. Calendar sync maps recurring tasks to Google Calendar events via separate OAuth scope."
  },
